package ui

// The two class names the stylesheet defines for the whole application, and the
// one component that has to carry one of them.
//
// They are declared here rather than in a `classes.go` because of a mechanical
// fact about the build: Tailwind scans `.templ` files and nothing else
// (`internal/web/static/css/app.css`'s `@source` directives), and a hand-written
// `.go` file under `components/` is invisible to it. Every class name this
// package's components render has to be visible to the scanner, so the
// declarations live beside the markup. A `.templ` file with no templ block is
// not an option either: templ writes an unconditional import of its runtime into
// every generated file, so a declaration-only `.templ` does not compile.

// TargetClass is the one class every interactive element carries.
//
// UI §7.3 enforces target size by construction rather than by review: a shared
// utility sets `min-inline-size: var(--target-min); min-block-size:
// var(--target-min)`, and every interactive element uses it — a plugin's
// included, because §4.11.1 makes the utility part of the plugin contract and
// §10.6's audit greps rendered markup without being able to tell whose output
// it is reading. A constant rather than a literal in each template so a test can
// assert the contract against the same name the markup uses, and so the
// stylesheet has one spelling to match.
const TargetClass = "target"

// SkipLinkClass is the class a skip link carries, and the hook the stylesheet's
// off-screen-until-focused rule targets.
//
// UI §7.2 fixes the skip links as the first focusable elements in the document,
// and `components.Shell` already renders them. This is the contract for the
// class and the component below is the same anchor it renders, so a future shell
// replaces two inline anchors with SkipLink and the served markup is unchanged.
const SkipLinkClass = "skip-link"

// SkipLink renders one skip link: a document's first focusable element, pointing
// at a landmark this route actually renders.
//
// The target is a bare id because UI §7.2's targets are real focusable elements
// carrying `tabindex="-1"`, so activating the link moves focus somewhere a screen
// reader announces rather than to the top of a scroll container. A caller may
// only pass an id this document renders: a link to a landmark that is not here
// moves focus nowhere, which is why §4.6 removes the campaign-navigation link
// from a pre-campaign route rather than leaving it inert.
templ SkipLink(target, label, testID string) {
	<a class={ SkipLinkClass + " " + TargetClass } href={ "#" + target } data-testid={ testID }>{ label }</a>
}